{"id":"78e7c924-89e7-465d-b81b-620a56cc15e7","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"1eb2b294c7ae42ad","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/build/eslint-toolchain.ts","baseline":{"blob":"fb9a26eabe4d3327ba55e4bc47a9e1551c9248cd","start":1815,"end":2185},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","FIXTURE","=","{","\"","tsconfig.json","\"",":","JSON",".","stringify","(","{","\"","compilerOptions","\"",":","{","\"","strict","\"",":","true",",","\"","target","\"",":","\"","ESNext","\"",",","\"","module","\"",":","\"","ESNext","\"",",","\"","moduleResolution","\"",":","\"","bundler","\"",",","\"","noEmit","\"",":","true","}",",","\"","include","\"",":","[","\"","src","\"","]","}",")",",","\"","src/probe.ts","\"",":","\"","async function load(): Promise<number> {\\n\\treturn 1;\\n}\\n\\nexport function run(): void {\\n\\tvar unused = 1;\\n\\tload();\\n\\tconsole.log(unused)\\n}\\n","\\","n","\\","t","\\","n","\\","n","\\","n","\\","n","\\","t","\\","n","\\","t","\\","n","\\","t","\\","n","\\","n","\"","}"]},"context":{"before":"28abee996da39a98","after":"c1bc1cb046a3b963"}},"payload":{"text":"The project the trace lints: a tsconfig (so typescript-eslint's project service, with types, is traced too) and a\nfile with something for type-aware and plain rules alike to say.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:09:11.714Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:09:11.714Z"}
{"id":"8374a6ef-d1d3-480e-8357-974bad2e8d4d","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"27023ffd2c4c98b6","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/build/eslint-toolchain.ts","baseline":{"blob":"54aa62f40a87ecc6a9bc23bb6d780b35329700a4","start":0,"end":46},"shape":{"type":"ImportDeclaration","atoms":["import","{","spawnSync","}","from","\"","node:child_process","\""]},"context":{"after":"bca5244780e81d0e"}},"payload":{"text":"The eslint worker's toolchain (extensions/eslint/worker.ts): ESLint, the preset (`@brianjenkins94/util/eslint`) and\neverything they load — typescript-eslint and TypeScript with its lib files among it — as one gzipped tar, served beside\nthe worker (`dist/lsp/eslint-toolchain.tgz`). The worker unpacks it into its own memory and runs ESLint from it under\nalmostnode, as Node would run it: no bundling, no polyfills of our own.\n\nWhat's in it is what a real lint loads: a child Node lints a small TypeScript project with the preset and traces every\nfile it loads or reads (eslint-toolchain-trace.mjs) — and of each package it loaded from, the whole package, less what\nnothing runs (source maps, type declarations, docs): a package may need a file the trace never read (one whose path\nit resolves as it loads, to start as a worker later, say). TypeScript is the exception, kept to what was read: its\ncompiler API and lib files, not its compiler and server.\n\nLaid out as npm lays out node_modules, whatever installed them here (npm's folders on a desktop, pnpm's symlinks into\nits store in CI — and the worker's filesystem has no symlinks): each package where Node finds it from the packages\nthat depend on it — one copy of a name at the top, another version of it under the package that needs that one.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:09:17.964Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:09:17.964Z"}
{"id":"881a8a6f-233f-4c03-8cc6-b9d7d4256d72","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"d37483d9736ca688","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/build/eslint-toolchain.ts","baseline":{"blob":"56f1de4149e1376a09a4015cbb07a31f74e72b93","start":3065,"end":3371},"shape":{"type":"FunctionDeclaration","atoms":["function","filesOf","(","root",":","string",")",":","string","[]","{","return","fs",".","readdirSync","(","root",",","{","\"","withFileTypes","\"",":","true","}",")",".","flatMap","(","(","entry",")","=>","{","const","full","=","path",".","join","(","root",",","entry",".","name",")",";","if","(","entry",".","isDirectory","(",")",")","{","return","entry",".","name","===","\"","node_modules","\"","?","[","]",":","filesOf","(","full",")",";","}","return","entry",".","isFile","(",")","?","[","full","]",":","[","]",";","}",")",";","}"]},"context":{"before":"1c4bde6a29a2ea55","after":"8fb169cbcf97c7c1"}},"payload":{"text":"A package's files (none in its own node_modules: each dependency is its own entry).","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:09:07.467Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:09:07.467Z"}
